  "directives": [
    "Long-form consistency is a prime directive and may veto local quality gains.",
    "Every material artifact may be inspected at its smallest useful atom while retaining full parent context.",
    "Every rival round is exactly construct -> attack/improve -> reconcile/promote, with roles rotating each round.",
    "Forge-100, Forge-1000 and Forge-10000 use exact round counts and no wall-clock deadline.",
    "Time is an ally through checkpointed iteration, never through unbounded resource growth.",
    "All game-related source classes are provenance- and rights-classified before use.",
    "Unknown rights are quarantined; reference-only sources may inform facts/techniques/ideas but not protected expression.",
    "Similarity checks are risk screens, not legal determinations; ambiguous cases escalate to human/legal review.",
    "No level may self-sign or count prose as completion evidence."
  ],
  "completion_rule": "A GBL level completes only with exact-head implementation plus its declared deterministic/adversarial/recovery/rights evidence; plan prose, rival confidence, round count or elapsed time alone never completes or signs a level.",
  "promotion_rule": "Stage-10 promotion requires independent evidence, all hard gates green, and exact binding to artifact/canon/source/model/tool/evaluator/effort identities.",
